{"annotationScore": 5.0, "comments": [{"commentType": "FUNCTION", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "10754382", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "11217080", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "26222560", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "id": "10754382", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Cleaves the alpha-chain at multiple sites and the beta-chain between 'Lys-53' and 'Lys-54' but not the gamma-chain of fibrinogen and therefore does not initiate the formation of the fibrin clot and does not cause the fibrinolysis directly (PubMed:11217080). It does not cleave (activate) prothrombin and plasminogen but converts the inactive single chain urinary plasminogen activator (pro-urokinase) to the active two chain form (PubMed:10754382, PubMed:11217080). Activates coagulation factor VII (Probable). May function as a tumor suppressor negatively regulating cell proliferation and cell migration (PubMed:26222560)"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBUNIT", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "11379758", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "8827452", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Heterodimer; disulfide-linked. Heterodimer of a 50 kDa heavy and a 27 kDa light chain linked by a disulfide bond"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "note": {"texts": [{"value": "Secreted as an inactive single-chain precursor and is then activated to a heterodimeric form"}]}, "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "8827452", "source": "PubMed"}], "id": "SL-0243", "value": "Secreted"}}]}, {"commentType": "ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS", "events": ["Alternative splicing"], "isoforms": [{"isoformIds": ["Q14520-1"], "isoformSequenceStatus": "Displayed", "name": {"value": "1"}}, {"isoformIds": ["Q14520-2"], "isoformSequenceStatus": "Described", "name": {"value": "2"}, "sequenceIds": ["VSP_044583"]}]}, {"commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "8827452", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Ubiquitously expressed"}]}, {"commentType": "PTM", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "11379758", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "8827452", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Proteolytic cleavage at Gly-23 or Met-27 can give rise to the 50 kDa heavy chain (HC) and cleavage at Arg-313 or Lys-319 can give rise to the 27 kDa light chain (LC) (PubMed:8827452). The HC can undergo further proteolytic cleavage giving rise to a 26 kDa fragment (PubMed:11379758). The LC can undergo further proteolytic cleavage at Arg-313 leading to a 17-kDa fragment and at Arg-480 leading to a 8-kDa fragment (PubMed:11379758)"}]}, {"commentType": "DISEASE", "disease": {"acronym": "NMTC5", "description": "A form of non-medullary thyroid cancer (NMTC), a cancer characterized by tumors originating from the thyroid follicular cells. NMTCs represent approximately 95% of all cases of thyroid cancer and are classified into papillary, follicular, Hurthle cell, and anaplastic neoplasms.", "diseaseAccession": "DI-04531", "diseaseCrossReference": {"database": "MIM", "id": "616535"}, "diseaseId": "Thyroid cancer, non-medullary, 5", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "12578864", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "26222560", "source": "PubMed"}]}, "note": {"texts": [{"value": "Disease susceptibility is associated with variants affecting the gene represented in this entry"}]}}, {"commentType": "SIMILARITY", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "id": "PRU00274", "source": "PROSITE-ProRule"}], "value": "Belongs to the peptidase S1 family"}]}], "entryAudit": {"entryVersion": 206, "firstPublicDate": "2005-08-30", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-11-04", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "1996-11-01", "sequenceVersion": 1}, "entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "extraAttribute